From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Oliver Sargison <sargo@sargo.cc>
Date: Tue, 27 Oct 2026 11:45:56 +1300
Subject: [PATCH 32/51] Plutonium: the dock in the sidebar, above the settings
 row

One button per slot, wrapping to the sidebar's width: the slot's icon (the
terminal, the app's own, a globe for a site) and its number, dimmed when
nothing of it runs in its scope, ringed when it shows. A click runs the slot
as Super+N does, and clicking the one that shows goes back (or puts it away
when there's nowhere to go back to). A right click puts the panel's tab or
the terminal there, keeps an app per thread, per project or everywhere, sets
the layout, or clears it. Panel tabs in the dock show their slot's number.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
